.Dd October 28, 2026
.Dt VINITCTL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vinitctl
.Nd control the vinit service supervisor
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm status
.Op Ar service
.Nm
.Cm list
.Nm
.Cm start | stop | restart
.Ar service
.Nm
.Cm reload
.Nm
.Cm reboot | poweroff | halt
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
sends one command to
.Xr vinit 8
and prints the reply.
Any user may run
.Cm status
and
.Cm list .
All other commands need uid 0.
.Bl -tag -width "restart service"
.It Cm status Op Ar service
Without
.Ar service ,
print the number of services in each state.
With
.Ar service ,
print its state, pid, type, restart count, last exit status and error.
.It Cm list
Print one line per service.
.It Cm start Ar service
Start
.Ar service
and the services it requires.
.It Cm stop Ar service
Stop the services that require
.Ar service ,
then stop
.Ar service .
.It Cm restart Ar service
Restart
.Ar service .
Services that depend on it keep running.
.It Cm reload
Read
.Pa /etc/vinit/services
again.
New services start, changed services restart, and unchanged services
keep running.
The reload is all or nothing: it is refused, and nothing changes, if it
would put a working service into an error state, or remove a service
that is still active.
.It Cm reboot , poweroff , halt
Shut down the system.
.El
.Pp
.Cm start ,
.Cm stop
and
.Cm restart
return as soon as
.Xr vinit 8
accepts the command.
Run
.Nm
.Cm status
to follow progress.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /run/vinit/control -compact
.It Pa /run/vinit/control
Control socket.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
Success.
.It 1
.Xr vinit 8
reported an error.
.It 2
Usage error, or no connection to
.Xr vinit 8 .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Edit a service file, then apply the change:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# vinitctl reload
# vinitctl status sshd
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr vinit.conf 5 ,
.Xr vinit 8
